artifact.self_contained_problem:
Let $\mathbb{D}=\{z\in\mathbb{C}:|z|<1\}$ denote the open unit disc, and let $\ell\ge 1$ be a fixed integer. Consider the family $\mathcal{F}$ of all functions $f$ meromorphic on $\mathbb{D}$ such that:
\begin{itemize}
\item $f(z)\neq 0$ for every $z\in\mathbb{D}$, and
\item $f^{(\ell)}(z)\neq 1$ for every $z\in\mathbb{D}$.
\end{itemize}
Determine whether $\mathcal{F}$ is a normal family on $\mathbb{D}$ in the sense of Montel (with respect to the spherical metric); that is, decide whether every sequence $\{f_n\}\subset\mathcal{F}$ contains a subsequence converging locally uniformly on $\mathbb{D}$ either to a meromorphic function or to $\infty$.

